course: dictionary
lesson: 4773
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words and sentences around them, tells you which meaning the writer wants. «Howler monkeys roar at dawn to tell other groups where their territory is.» Here a howler is an animal, a monkey that howls.
explain: «Writing "the Pacific Ocean is in Paris" is a howler.» Now a howler is a silly, obvious mistake, the kind that makes people laugh. The clue is the writing: nobody is howling, but someone has made an error.
explain: To choose the right meaning, ask what the sentence is about. Is it about monkeys, a sound, or a mistake? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A howler can mean a silly, obvious mistake, often a funny one, especially in writing or an exam.
fact: A howler can also mean an animal or person that howls, such as a howler monkey.
fact: A howler monkey is a large monkey from South and Central America with a very loud call.
fact: Howler monkeys have a large hollow bone in the throat, which helps their call carry about 5 kilometres.
fact: In the Harry Potter books a Howler is a magic red letter that yells at its reader. This meaning is old-fashioned.
exercise: «Writing "the Pacific Ocean is in Paris" is a howler.» What does howler mean here? | *A silly, obvious mistake | An animal that howls | A type of letter | A loud wind at night
exercise: «Howler monkeys roar at dawn to tell other groups where their territory is.» What is a howler monkey? | A small, quiet bird | A type of spider | A tool for cracking nuts | *A large South and Central American monkey with a very loud call
exercise: «A large hollow bone in the throat makes the boom.» What makes the howler's boom? | Its two hands | *A large hollow bone in the throat | A stone it holds | Its long tail
test: Ella writes "the Pacific Ocean is in Paris" in her test, and the teacher laughs. What has she made? | A troop | *A howler | A howl | A boom
test: Why do howler monkeys roar at dawn? | To sleep longer | *To tell other groups where their territory is | To catch a sloth | To cool down in hot springs
exam: In «howlers boom at dawn», what does boom suggest? | A silly mistake | *A deep, very loud sound | A quiet sound | A letter that yells
